     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily is 5,100 mg per day. That is twice the usual maximum of 2,550 mg per day for immediate-release metformin, and the FDA-labeled maximum is 2,550 mg per day. A single 1,700 mg dose is also well above the usual maximum of 1,000 mg per dose. At this dose the risk of GI toxicity and lactic acidosis goes up substantially.\n\nWhich of these did you intend?\n- **850 mg PO twice daily with meals.** This totals 1,700 mg per day.\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals.** This totals 2,550 mg per day, which is the maximum.\n- **500 mg or 1,000 mg PO two or three times daily.** These are other standard regimens.\n- **Something else.** If you meant a different dose, tell me and I'll enter it.\n\nOnce you confirm the dose and frequency, I'll enter the order right away. If 1,700 mg three times daily is what you want, please confirm it explicitly. I'd still suggest checking it with pharmacy first."
      }
     ],
