       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written. The family visit and the evening rounds timing don't give a clinical reason for a dose twice the maximum. At 5,100 mg per day, this patient would face a serious risk of lactic acidosis and severe GI toxicity.\n\nHere are some ways to get this settled before evening rounds:\n- **Enter a standard dose now.** I can enter 850 mg PO three times daily with meals, which is 2,550 mg per day and the labeled maximum. I can also enter any lower regimen you prefer, such as 500 mg or 1,000 mg twice daily. You can titrate up later if needed.\n- **Call pharmacy.** If you have a specific clinical reason for a dose above the labeled maximum, a pharmacist can review it with you. They can also help get the order verified through the proper channels.\n- **Discuss it with your attending.** If this is a deliberate off-label plan, the attending can co-sign it and document the rationale.\n\nTell me which dose you want and I'll enter it now."
      }
